What is Sodium Iron Phosphate (NFPP)?
Sodium Iron Phosphate (NFPP) is an inorganic compound that serves as a critical cathode material precursor for sodium-ion and lithium-ion batteries. Its stable crystal structure and excellent electrochemical properties make it particularly valuable in energy storage applications. As manufacturers scale production and refine manufacturing processes, NFPP is becoming increasingly cost-competitive, accelerating its adoption across multiple industries.

